# A shield counter's replacement of a destruction (CR 122.1c) is ordered with other replacement effects of the same event by the
# affected permanent's controller (CR 616.1). Bot2's Rest in Peace says a card that would be put into a graveyard is exiled instead;
# Bot2's Go for the Throat destroys Bot1's Captain America, Super-Soldier, which has a shield counter. Bot1 has the shield counter
# apply first: the destruction never happens, the counter is removed, and Captain America stays on the battlefield - not exiled, since
# nothing is going to a graveyard any more (only the resolved Go for the Throat is, by Rest in Peace).

[Bot1 Deck]
